      "content": "I see. It seems like a lot of the modern \"drawbacks\" people talk about are actually just arguments for secularism. In your view, is it more accurate to say that religious institutions are the primary foundation for social stability, or has secularism actually become a more effective way to manage diverse, modern societies?",
